    "q-164474": {
      "dom_id": "step-q164474",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Identify the following surface: \n\n$$\n(x+1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}-(z-1)^{2}=1\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the equation of a hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $O$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=1,\n$$\n\nand a hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}}-\\frac{(z-{z}_{0})^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=1,\n$$\n\nThus, our equation is a hyperboloid of one sheet with the following parameters:\n\n$$\n({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(-1,3,1),\\,a=b=c=1.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-164474-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "An ellipsoid",
              "html": "An ellipsoid"
            },
            {
