    "q-164542": {
      "dom_id": "step-q164542",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Identify the following surface:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{5}=1,\\,-\\infty <y<\\infty .\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the equation of a hyperbolic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nThus, a hyperbolic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $y$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is a hyperbolic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $y$-axis and $a=1,\\,c=\\sqrt{5}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
